From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Use grep -F instead of obsolete fgrep

Recent grep prints a deprecation warning for fgrep.  The directory
comparison test expects no output, so use the equivalent grep -F form
without changing the paths being compared.

Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
diff --git a/src/sanity.sh b/src/sanity.sh
--- a/src/sanity.sh
+++ b/src/sanity.sh
@@ -1723,9 +1723,9 @@
 	cd $DIR_1
-	find . -print | fgrep -v /CVS | sort > $TESTDIR/dc$$d1
+	find . -print | grep -F -v /CVS | sort > $TESTDIR/dc$$d1
 
 	# go back where we were to avoid symlink hell...
 	cd $OLDPWD
 	cd $DIR_2
-	find . -print | fgrep -v /CVS | sort > $TESTDIR/dc$$d2
+	find . -print | grep -F -v /CVS | sort > $TESTDIR/dc$$d2
 
 	if diff $TESTDIR/dc$$d1 $TESTDIR/dc$$d2 >/dev/null 2>&1
